@startuml
' component.puml
!theme plain
title Component Architecture — Shift Schedule Notification Bot
' Pattern: Adapter | Sprint 001 | 2026-04-05

' ===== File System Artifacts =====
file "~/.env\n(secrets/config)" as env
file "~/schedule.xlsx\n(read-only)" as xlsx
file "~/shift_bot.db\n(SQLite)" as sqlitedb
folder "~/logs/\n(timestamped log files)" as logs

' ===== External Messenger APIs =====
rectangle "External Systems" as extSys {
  component [Telegram Bot API] as tgAPI
  component [Viber Bot API]    as vbAPI
}

' ===== Application Boundary =====
rectangle "Application  (Python, venv, one-shot script)" as app {

  component [main.py\nOrchestrator] as main
  component [cli.py\nCLI & Mode Parser] as cli
  note right of cli
    Parses sys.argv, returns mode object.
    Modes: health | dry-run | production |
           reload-schedule.
    No message ever sent without --production.
  end note

  component [config.py\nConfig & Startup Validation] as config
  note right of config
    Loads all env variables at startup.
    Missing variable → log error, exit(1).
    No further execution with broken config.
  end note

  component [db.py\nSQLite Layer] as db
  note right of db
    Creates shift_bot.db on first run.
    Schema: notifications, receipts.
    Only db.py may read/write the DB.
    No SQL in any other module.
  end note

  component [schedule_parser.py\nXLSX Parser] as parser
  note right of parser
    Reads schedule.xlsx on every run.
    Returns typed list of Shift objects.
    No network calls, no side effects.
  end note

  component [shift_logic.py\nPure Shift Logic] as logic
  note right of logic
    Sorts shifts by date/time.
    Finds prev/next colleague
    per employee by (role, location).
    Pure functions only — fully unit-testable,
    zero I/O, zero network calls.
  end note

  package "messenger/" as messengerPkg {
    interface "MessengerGateway\n<<interface>>" as gw
    component [telegram_adapter.py\nTelegram REST — P1] as tgA
    component [viber_adapter.py\nViber REST — P2 deferred] as vbA
    note bottom of messengerPkg
      DEPENDENCY LOCALITY RULE:
      Only telegram_adapter.py and viber_adapter.py
      may call external messenger REST endpoints.
      main.py, shift_logic.py, schedule_parser.py
      must NEVER call requests to messenger APIs directly.
    end note
  }
}

' ===== Boot Sequence (orchestrated by main.py) =====
' Steps 1-4 must all succeed before any message is sent.
' Step 5 must complete for ALL employees before Step 6 begins.
main --> cli     : "parse flags → mode"
main --> config  : "① load & validate config"
main --> db      : "② init DB / verify schema"
main --> gw      : "③ init messenger sessions"
main --> parser  : "④ parse schedule.xlsx"
main --> logic   : "⑤ compute prev/next shifts"
main --> gw      : "⑥ dispatch messages"
main --> logs    : "⑦ write summary log"

' ===== Internal Wiring =====
config ..> env  : reads
parser ..> xlsx : reads
db     ..> sqlitedb : reads/writes

gw <|.. tgA : implements
gw <|.. vbA : implements

' ===== Dependency Locality — ONLY adapters touch REST =====
tgA --> tgAPI : "REST sendMessage"
vbA --> vbAPI : "REST send_message"

@enduml
